From 0ab25908db1d6e51bc586b9269ee75a67c14029d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:02:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 116/638] [AROS] Normalize executable names from DOS

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-3
AI_STATUS: implementation
ROOT_CAUSE: GetProgramName returned the invoked command path Developer:Chromium/headless_shell, while GetProgramDir already resolved System:Developer/Chromium; concatenating both produced a duplicated DIR_ASSETS path and hid the headless resource packs.
FIX_REASON: Reduce the DOS program string to its FilePart basename before joining it to the locked program directory.
SCOPE: base/base_paths_aros.cc
VALIDATION: base_paths_aros.o cross-compiled; hosted 0116 logged failed lookups under System:Developer/Chromium/Developer:Chromium and then aborted after locale resources remained empty.
RISK: Low; FILE_EXE and FILE_MODULE retain the resolved program directory and now consistently use the executable basename regardless of invocation syntax.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: PartitionAlloc pools initialized -> headless command starts -> duplicated DIR_ASSETS -> normalize AROS program basename
Continues: 3e42c47a8e
---
 base/base_paths_aros.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/base/base_paths_aros.cc b/base/base_paths_aros.cc
index cf86eed0c7..f0a911a9cb 100644
--- a/base/base_paths_aros.cc
+++ b/base/base_paths_aros.cc
@@ -27,10 +27,14 @@ bool GetExecutablePath(FilePath* result) {
     return false;
   }
 
+  const char* program_name = FilePart(program);
+  if (!program_name || !*program_name)
+    program_name = program;
+
   std::string path(directory);
   if (!path.empty() && path.back() != ':' && path.back() != '/')
     path.push_back('/');
-  path.append(program);
+  path.append(program_name);
   *result = FilePath(path);
   return true;
 }
